for the past decade or more the Marvel  Cinematic Universe has dominated the box  office and pop culture as a whole but  sandwiched in between the MCU mega  blockbusters Captain Marvel and Avengers  endgame there's another little superhero  movie from the underdogs at DC Comics  and it's actually really awesome how  awesome well here's a spoiler filled  look at the four best and for worse  things about Shazam the films that the  DC extended universe have a well-earned  reputation for being dark grim and  gritty which a lot of audiences felt  weren't too much fun to watch there's a  lot of angst and moral ambivalence and  very little in the way of actual heroism  instead they seem to feature angry  people who clearly aren't getting enough  fiber in their diets so maybe the  biggest surprise about Shazam is that  it's not just funny it's also actually  fun from start to finish  director David F Sandberg mostly does a  great job keeping the tone upbeat and  energetic as team Billy Batson discovers  his incredible new powers it's true that  Aquaman also dared to have at least a  good time along the way but Billy's  exuberance at becoming a superhero is  something we haven't really seen before  and it's a welcome change compared to  the DCE use usual dark and violent fair  did you believe yeah on the other hand  while Shazam is mostly family-friendly  fun once in awhile it just sort of  forgets itself and beers off into the  realm of horror of course this makes  some sense considering that Sandberg is  best known for directing the acclaimed  horror hits lights out and Annabel  creation still the total shifts are  jarring one minute Billy and his foster  brother Freddy Freeman are clowning  around doing the floss and then the next  minute the evil dr. sivana is summoning  a horde of demons to literally eat  people's heads off oh snap you're like a  bad guy right these abrupt detours into  terror feel kinda out of place and  unnecessary luckily it doesn't happen  often but even a couple of times might  be a couple of times too many across the  board the stars of Shazam deliver and  then some Zachary Levi is the super  heroic adult form that young Billy takes  maintains a level of boyish wonder while  using his grown-up physicality to great  effect he also has a terrific rapport  with Jack Dillon grazer as Billy's  foster brother Freddie Freeman and  grazer similarly has excellent chemistry  with ash or angel who plays the younger  less mighty mortal version of Billy it's  hard enough for most movies to find even  one star that's right for any given part  but Shazam somehow nailed the casting  for its three biggest roles and the  movie is much better for it still not  every role comes off as well as it could  have and one area where the movie really  falls short is its villains that's not  actually a knock on actor Mark Strong  who plays the lead villain dr. thaddeus  sivana strong has a long history of  playing baddies and films and he's very  good at being very bad but unfortunately  while all the stuff with billy and  freddie feels fresh and new the scenes  with dr. sivana feel like they were  cobbled together from a list of boring  supervillain cliches plus his demonic  cgi helpers have boring designs the  coolest saying Shazam did with villains  was teasing mr. mind an evil genius worm  in the mid-credits scene we just wish he  had been the lead villain of this one  too at least that wouldn't have been  just more of the same when movie makers  don't respect the comics their films are  based on the result is always bad and  always disappointing just look at films  like Jonah Hex or even Man of Steel  which was controversial among longtime  comic book fans in that one many have  said that director Zack Snyder didn't  believe the concept of a pure hero like  Superman was relevant the impulse to  make comic book movies more serious  because the filmmakers want to be taken  seriously is never a good thing which is  why it's so great that Shazam actually  rebels and it's comic book origins the  filmmakers don't mind being goofy  because they know it's fine as long as  audiences are brought along for the ride  characters like mr. mind or silly but  they're exactly the kind of silly we've  been waiting for all along Shazam is  trying to do a lot of different things  it's got comedy it's got action it's got  a heartwarming family message at its  gooey center and it's a modern superhero  fable but while it does most of these  things pretty well trying to do them all  at once results in a movie going  experience that's kind of like trying to  eat a Chipotle burrito it's just over  stopped and that over ambition shows in  the film's runtime for a fast paced fun  movie  Shazaam isn't actually all that  fast-paced instead it runs a whopping  two hours and twelve minutes which is  maybe a half hour too long Shazaam is  really good but like the old saying goes  sometimes you can get too much of a good  thing  a little restraints would have been  better for the movie and better for your  bladder superpowers dude I don't even  know how to pee in this thing like all  good films Shazam is actually about  something more than simple superhero  fist fights at the heart of the film is  young Billy Batson and his quest to find  his family in the end he realizes his  true family was right in front of him  all along it's a great art made all the  better by the performances of the actors  who play his foster siblings especially  faith Herman as the precocious Darla  even better the twist ending where all  of his siblings are granted the powers  of the wizard Shazam is a great callback  to the comics scene Billy and his  siblings come together to fight crime  was a great surprise that delivered both  the action and the fields at the same  time about the only thing that could  have made the superhero family twist  even better was if we hadn't already  known it was coming  so who spoiled it for everyone no it  wasn't some paparazzi or gossip websites  instead it's the modern scourge of film  fans everywhere merchandise tie-ins yes  unfortunately images of the action  figures released months before the  film's April release spoiling the  surprise  hey toy companies next time could you  please keep it zipped until after the  movie is out check out one of our newest  videos right here plus even more looper  videos about your favorite superhero  movies are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]  [Applause]
 

